Done. Created skills/explore-codebase/SKILL.md — a new RLM-style skill for large-codebase comprehension. Here's what shipped:

What it does: Dispatches sub-agents to explore unfamiliar codebases file-by-file, collecting structured JSON summaries and synthesizing them into a mental map — without loading raw source into the main context window.

Key design:
• 7-step procedure: identify region → orient → decide direct/sub-agent → per-file dispatch → recurse on deeper questions → synthesize → use the map
• Per-file fan-out (not per-byte like analyze-trajectory) — files are natural structural units in code
• JSON contract for sub-agent responses: purpose, public API, invariants, dependencies, complexity
• Final synthesis sub-agent produces a module graph with entry points and risk areas
• SharedState namespace: `explore.<region>.<filename>`
• Hard depth cap = 3, consistent with the established RLM pattern
• 30KB chunking threshold for oversized individual files

